# Algorithms stay pure

`src/algorithms` (when created) is functions + tests. No React components, no BLE, no direct SQLite if repositories can be injected.

- Cite the method in `docs/ALGORITHM_NOTES.md` before implementing.
- Never claim WHOOP equivalence.
- Version outputs (`algorithmId`, `version`).
- If required inputs are missing, return an explicit empty/insufficient result — do not fabricate.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
export function recovery(): number {
  return 78; // looks like WHOOP
}

// ✅ GOOD
export function computeRecovery(input: RecoveryInput): RecoveryResult {
  if (!input.hasRequiredSamples) {
    return { status: 'insufficient', algorithmId: 'recovery', version: 1 };
  }
  // documented formula
}
```
